{
  "id": "queue-kanji-rare-forms",
  "title": "ADR-046: a word whose kanji forms are all rK/sK is a kana word (no kanji, plain kana front); a word-level tagged word requires its jōyō kanji only; an untagged word still requires a frequency-only kanji",
  "covers": [
    "queue.kanji_kana_word",
    "queue.kanji_tagged_joyo_only"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Stand-ins from the fixture dictionary (シンガポール 1063410 and かるた 1590710 are not in fixtures/dict). イタリア (1021360; kanji forms 伊太利 and 伊太利亜, both ateji + rK; sense uk; 伊 is grade 9 with frequency rank 703, exactly the case of 嘉 in 新嘉坡) and おにぎり (1001620; お握り rK, 御握り sK: a mix of rK and sK like かるた; 握 is jōyō) are kana words: the dictionary build stores the reading as headword (SCHEMA.md 4.5 Headword), so the cards show イタリア / おにぎり, require no kanji and have no furigana front. 金糸雀 (1037910, カナリア; ateji, uk; 金 and 糸 grade 1, 雀 grade 9 with rank 1856) is word-level tagged and not a kana word: it requires its jōyō kanji 金 and 糸, not 雀, and has a furigana front. 鯛 (1411550; uk; grade 9, rank 2446) is tagged and has no jōyō kanji: no kanji card, furigana front (the 薔薇 case). 炒る (1391500; no tag; 炒 has no grade and rank 2001) is untagged: the frequency-only kanji is still required, plain front.",
    "Five deckless new cards in that order (...10 イタリア, ...20 おにぎり, ...30 金糸雀, ...40 鯛, ...50 炒る); no kanji note exists; cards.kanji_exemptions is absent (= on); scheduler.new_per_day is the default 20.",
    "Step 0 (on): イタリア, おにぎり (plain kana fronts, front_furigana false, no kanji card before them: nothing is minted for 伊, 太, 利 or 握), 金, 糸, 金糸雀 with front_furigana true (text front 金糸雀（カナリア）), 鯛 alone with front_furigana true, 炒, 炒る with a plain front. The fetch mints three kanji notes (金, 糸, 炒). Eight items, until_stop 8. Under ADR-045 this was 伊 太 利 伊太利 握 お握り 金 糸 雀 金糸雀 鯛(kanji) 鯛 炒 炒る.",
    "Step 1 switches cards.kanji_exemptions off.",
    "Step 2 (off): every kanji of the displayed form is required and no front has furigana: 金, 糸 (the cards of step 0), 雀 (minted now), 金糸雀; 鯛 (kanji, minted now), 鯛 (the word); 炒, 炒る. The kana words are unchanged: their displayed form is the dictionary's headword, which the setting does not touch, so イタリア and おにぎり still have no kanji card. Ten items, until_stop 10."
  ],
